_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/68558-looking-for-geists-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view?p=72409#post72409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well said, mind if I quote it for my signature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Side note. They don't necessarily go away if you kill them enough times. While they're no longer PC material, they could just end up as one of the.. umm... whatever word for Synergy 0 bound is. Where is a true split personality running around doing things.<br /> <br /> Meaning that if its the Geist half that's angry at you, you're still in trouble. The only way known to actually put down one of the bound with 100 percent accuracy is the Sin Eater ritual that cuts away the Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2014, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T16:37:48-08:00","id":84917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/68558-looking-for-geists-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view#post68558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> So I was hoping to feature the occasional Krewe in a game I'm running sooner or later, but have only middling familiarity and none of the books. I didn't want to have to retcon anything if a later player wanted to play one of them or get more involved. I'm shooting for a persistent setting (centralized on Huntsville, Alabama, if that makes any difference), and wanted to do them right.<br /> <br /> So what I'm asking for, could someone give me an overview of what kinds of groups there are, what Geists can *do*, and why/when they do it. I'd like to involve more groups than just the &quot;good guys&quot; (if there are any), I don't want to limit myself to the stereotypically &quot;Player&quot; groups or &quot;Enemy&quot; groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, if you can, I'd highly recommend getting the book. The fluff is downright stuffed with idea-fodder, the art is gorgeous (if somewhat monochromatic, but it works), and it's a good reference on ghosts and the like. You should be able to <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/64033/Geist-The-SinEaters\" target=\"_blank\">get it off DriveThru</a> easily enough, and you really won't regret it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/68558-looking-for-geists-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view?p=72581#post72581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note. They don't necessarily go away if you kill them enough times. While they're no longer PC material, they could just end up as one of the.. umm... whatever word for Synergy 0 bound is. Where is a true split personality running around doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wretched they are called, and Wretched they really are. Poor bastards...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}